  "summary": "Senators Sanders, Merkley and Rep. Ocasio-Cortez introduced the Ban Flock Act, which would bar federal agencies from using ALPRs and withhold federal funding from state/local governments that use them. Separately, Sen. Hawley introduced the Stop Flock Abuse Act requiring written search approvals, 10-day data deletion, and banning facial recognition integration; Reps. Casar and Brown wrote to the FBI about its ALPR acquisition plans.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "the Ban Flock Act, which would prohibit federal agencies from using automatic license plate readers (ALPRs) and block federal funding from state and local governments that use the cameras",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "The Stop Flock Abuse Act would require a written approval process for each search; force agencies to delete driver data after ten days, with exceptions for active investigations; and ban ALPR networks from incorporating facial recognition technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
